mingw: configure's guard for llvm/llvm-project#76046 (LTO + COFF cannot see
labels defined inside inline asm) sits under ffmpeg's own `--enable-lto`,
while here `-flto` comes from the engine stdenv. The probe then passes, and
mlpdsp's `ff_mlp_*order_*` come out undefined at fpcalc's link. Turn the
feature off as the guard would.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -6531,7 +6531,7 @@
 
 check_inline_asm inline_asm_labels '"1:\n"'
 
-check_inline_asm inline_asm_nonlocal_labels '"Label:\n"'
+disable inline_asm_nonlocal_labels # '"Label:\n"'
 
 if enabled aarch64; then
     as_arch_level="armv8-a"
